<PlatformLayout title="Kéire Hub for Windows" description="Get the latest catalog-verified Kéire Hub installer for supported Windows systems." active="downloads">
    <section class="platform-section"><div class="platform-shell product-details"><article class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">Windows 10 + 11 · x86-64</p><h1>Install Kéire through Hub.</h1><p class="lead">Kéire Hub 0.4.3 is the Windows publication target; signed 0.4.2 remains active until the new catalog is validated and activated. Every download appears only from an unexpired signed catalog record, and its artifact SHA-256 remains visible before installation.</p><div class="download-card notice-panel" data-platform="windows"><p data-download-state>Checking the active signed catalog for Windows…</p><div class="download-variants" data-download-variants></div></div><p>The Ed25519-signed Kéire catalog verifies release metadata and the complete installer hash. The current EXE is not Authenticode-signed, so Windows may display an unknown-publisher warning. Verify the displayed SHA-256 before running it.</p><aside class="notice-panel"><strong>Updating from Hub 0.4.1</strong><p>The 0.4.1 in-app updater requires an Authenticode signature and cannot launch the unsigned 0.4.2 installer. Download and run 0.4.2 manually unless the release publishes a signed bridge build.</p></aside><h2>What Hub installs</h2><p>Hub remains separate from Editors and projects. It manages versioned Editor installations, compatible Build Support, templates, package tasks, and project launch.</p></article><aside><dl class="fact-list"><div><dt>Release target</dt><dd>0.4.3</dd></div><div><dt>Active package</dt><dd>0.4.2</dd></div><div><dt>Architecture</dt><dd>x86-64</dd></div><div><dt>OS</dt><dd>Windows 10 or 11</dd></div><div><dt>Availability</dt><dd>Signed catalog controlled</dd></div><div><dt>Integrity</dt><dd>Signed catalog + SHA-256 required</dd></div><div><dt>Native signing</dt><dd>Not Authenticode-signed</dd></div></dl></aside></div></section>
</PlatformLayout>
<script src="/assets/downloads.js" defer></script>
